From e4fee14f0f8d1f355c9c45d532657343ebc069d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:06:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Match requests with a trie over the route table

Dispatch tried each route in turn, so its cost grew with the table. toHandler and Router.toHandler now build a segment trie once. One walk of it collects the routes that could match the path, or the path with a trailing slash added. Route.tryMatch then runs on those routes in table order, both for the match and for the slash redirect.

RouteIndex.first_of and RouteIndex.wantsSlash_of prove that both answers equal what matchTable gives, for every table, method and path. RouteIndex.memory_of bounds the trie by one node per pattern segment, plus the root, with each route's index stored once. The trie lives in Routing.Internal, and the public functions keep their signatures.

Signed-off-by: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
